    "diagnosis": "",
    "title": "<p class=\"TableTitle\"><strong>Table&nbsp;1.02</strong> Pathogenesis, clinical features, and associated lymphoproliferative disorders across major categories of inborn errors of immunity (IEIs) of T&nbsp;and B&nbsp;cells <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{31953710;33598806}</span></p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "",
    "copyright": "Not necessary - all authors",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; mso-table-layout-alt: fixed; mso-yfti-tbllook: 1184; mso-padding-alt: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" border=\"0\" width=\"944\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 0; mso-yfti-firstrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 169.2pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"226\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>IEI subtype</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 177.3pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"236\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Pathogenesis</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 177.3pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"236\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Clinical features</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.35pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Lymphoproliferative disorders</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 1; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 708.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"5\" width=\"944\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Predominantly antibody deficiencies: 52% of IEIs worldwide </strong><span class=\"Ref-ID\">{32720819}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 2; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 27.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"37\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 141.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"188\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Common variable immunodeficiency (~35% of primary immunodeficiency disorders) <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{28606585}</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 177.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"236\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Marked decrease in &ge;&nbsp;2&nbsp;immunoglobulin subsets (IgG and either IgA, IgM, or both) often due to defects in B-cell development and maturation; altered T-cell repertoire <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{26311730;22042693;31942606;33256375}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 177.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"236\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Infections, autoimmunity, lymphoproliferation; lymphoma and gastric cancer predisposition</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.35pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">EBV+ or EBV&minus; DLBCL &gt;&nbsp;EBV+ CHL &gt;&nbsp;EMZL &gt;&nbsp;T-cell large granular lymphocyte leukaemia <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{32185577;34255892;33876323}</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Cutaneous and other extranodal CD8+ T-cell&ndash;rich lymphoid or lymphohistiocytic infiltrates</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 3; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 27.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"37\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 141.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"188\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Activated PI3K&delta; syndrome</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 177.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"236\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Abnormal T-lymphocyte signalling due to gain-of-function variants in <em>PIK3CD</em> <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{24165795}</span> or loss-of-function variants in <em>PIK3R1</em>, <em>PTEN</em> <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{31111319}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 177.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"236\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Lymphadenopathy, hepatosplenomegaly, nodular mucosal lymphoid hyperplasia, herpesvirus infections (EBV, CMV, herpes simplex virus)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">DLBCL &gt;&nbsp;CHL &gt;&nbsp;EMZL &gt;&nbsp;others; majority of DLBCLs and CHLs are EBV+ <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{27555459;27221134;31942637}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 4; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 27.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"37\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 141.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"188\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>HyperIgM syndrome</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 177.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"236\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Defective class-switch recombination, lack of germinal centres, e.g. activation-induced cytidine deaminase (AID) deficiency <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{33098766}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 177.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"236\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Bacterial infections, lymphadenopathy, plasmacytosis</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.35pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">DLBCL, CHL, EMZL <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{32192142}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 5; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 27.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"37\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 141.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"188\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Agammaglobulinaemia</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 177.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"236\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Decreased to absent B cells, e.g. variants in <em>BTK</em> (X-linked agammaglobulinaemia) <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{24909997}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 177.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"236\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Severe bacterial infections</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Lymphoma uncommon <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{33584693}</span><br />Rare cutaneous granulomatous CD8+ T-cell lymphoproliferative disorder <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{24813299}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 6; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 708.15pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"5\" width=\"944\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Combined immunodeficiencies: 10.8% of IEIs worldwide </strong><span class=\"Ref-ID\">{32720819}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 7; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 27.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"37\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 141.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"188\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Syndromic combined immunodeficiencies with predisposition to malignancy (AT, NBS)</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 177.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"236\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Pleiotropic DNA repair defects, e.g. <em>ATM</em> deficiency (AT) <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{25488969;7792600}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 177.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"236\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Infection, developmental abnormalities, radiation sensitivity (see <span class=\"ID-Section\">&lt;&lt;4.5.1&gt;&gt;</span><em>Ataxia&ndash;telangiectasia (ATM)</em>, and <span class=\"ID-Section\">&lt;&lt;4.5.3&gt;&gt;</span><em>Nijmegen breakage syndrome (NBN)</em>)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">AT: DLBCL, BL, CHL, T-LBL, rarely T-cell prolymphocytic leukaemia <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{25488969;31057537}</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">NBS: DLBCL &gt; T-LBL &gt; peripheral T-cell lymphoma &gt; others <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{33488600}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 8; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 27.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"37\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 141.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"188\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>SCID</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 177.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"236\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Defects in core T-cell development and signalling pathways or DNA recombination repair, e.g. <em>DCLRE1C</em> (<em>ARTEMIS</em>) deficiency <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{11336668}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 177.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"236\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Severe infection susceptibility; subset radiosensitive</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.35pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Lymphoma rarely reported, usually EBV+ DLBCL <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{31057537}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 9; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 27.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"37\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 141.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"188\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Leaky SCID, Omenn syndrome</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 177.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"236\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Hypomorphic versions of SCID e.g. <em>DCLRE1C</em> (<em>ARTEMIS</em>) deficiency <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{26476407}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 177.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"236\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span lang=\"FR\">Infection, adenopathy, rash, eosinophilia, granulomatous lesions</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span lang=\"FR\">EBV+ DLBCL <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{31057537}</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span lang=\"FR\">Rare cutaneous granulomatous CD8+ T-cell lymphoproliferative disorder <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{31313695}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 10; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 27.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"37\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span lang=\"FR\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 141.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"188\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Combined immunodeficiencies</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 177.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"236\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Defects in less-critical or downstream T-cell signalling pathways or cytoskeletal proteins e.g. <em>WAS</em> <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{12196287;26371186}</span>,&nbsp;<em><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-fareast-theme-font: minor-fareast; mso-ansi-language: EN-GB; mso-fareast-language: EN-GB; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA;\">CD40LG</span></em><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-fareast-theme-font: minor-fareast; mso-ansi-language: EN-GB; mso-fareast-language: EN-GB; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA;\"> (<em>CD154</em>)</span>&nbsp;deficiency <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{7679801;7678782}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 177.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"236\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Infection, autoimmunity; subset with thrombocytopenia (Wiskott&ndash;Aldrich syndrome)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.35pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">DLBCL &gt;&nbsp;BL &gt;&nbsp;CHL &gt;&nbsp;other, often EBV+ <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{31057537}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 11; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 27.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"37\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 141.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"188\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Thymic defects with additional congenital abnormalities</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 177.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"236\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Lack of thymic development with associated developmental abnormalities, e.g. del22q11.2 <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{32668295}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 177.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"236\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Infections, developmental abnormalities (e.g. velocardiofacial&nbsp;/ DiGeorge syndrome)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Rare case report of EBV+ B-cell lymphoma <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{31057537}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 12; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 27.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"37\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 141.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"188\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Immuno-osseous dysplasias</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 177.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"236\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Pleiotropic cellular defects, e.g. variants in <em>RMRP</em> (cartilage hair hypoplasia) <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{17701897}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 177.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"236\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Skeletal abnormalities, bone marrow failure, immune deficiency</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.35pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">B-cell lymphoma <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{31057537}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 13; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 27.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"37\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 141.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"188\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>HyperIgE syndromes</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 177.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"236\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">T-cell subset defects with dysregulated IgE production, e.g. <em>STAT3</em> (Job syndrome) <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{20159255}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 177.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"236\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">High IgE, pyogenic infections, skeletal/dental abnormalities</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">DLBCL &gt;&nbsp;CHL &gt;&nbsp;BL &gt;&nbsp;T-cell lymphoma; minority are EBV+ <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{20859667}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 14; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 708.15pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"5\" width=\"944\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Immune dysregulation</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 15; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 27.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"37\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 141.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"188\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Familial HLH syndromes <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{32542393}</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 177.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"236\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">T-cell hyperactivation leading to histiocyte activation, e.g. variants in <em>PRF1</em> (familial HLH&nbsp;2), <em>LYST</em> (Chediak&ndash;Higashi syndrome) <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{21878672}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 177.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"236\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">HLH, hepatosplenomegaly; Chediak&ndash;Higashi syndrome: hypopigmentation, platelet and neutrophil defects</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Predominance of HLH</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Lymphoma rare</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 16; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 27.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"37\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 141.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"188\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span lang=\"FR\">Autosomal dominant immune dysregulation syndrome</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 177.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"236\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em>CTLA4</em> dominant negative loss of function <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{25329329}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 177.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"236\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Autoimmunity, lymphoproliferation, infections</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.35pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Enriched for EBV+ CHL; CD4+ T-cell&ndash;rich extranodal infiltrates <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{30250467}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 17; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 27.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"37\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 141.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"188\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Regulatory T-cell defects</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 177.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"236\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Lack or dysfunction of CD4+ CD25+ regulatory T&nbsp;cells, increased autoreactive T&nbsp;cells, e.g. <em>FOXP3</em> deficiency (immune dysregulation, polyendocrinopathy, enteropathy, X-linked syndrome) <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{30443250}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 177.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"236\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Autoimmunity, lymphoproliferation, infections, inflammatory bowel disease</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Predominance of HLH</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Lymphoma rare</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 18; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 27.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"37\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 141.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"188\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span lang=\"FR\">ALPS (see <span class=\"ID-Section\">&lt;&lt;3.3.1&gt;&gt;</span><em>Autoimmune lymphoproliferative syndrome (FAS)</em>)</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 177.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"236\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span lang=\"FR\">Defective T-cell apoptosis, e.g. <em>FAS</em> (<em>TNFRSF6</em>) deficiency (ALPS-<em>FAS</em>) <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{33963613}</span>; many other variants result in an ALPS-like phenotype <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{34447369}</span>; <em>KRAS</em> and <em>NRAS</em> somatic mutations can produce an ALPS-like phenotype <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{21063026}</span> as well as myeloid manifestations <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{25691160;33011939}</span> (see <span class=\"ID-Section\">&lt;&lt;3.3.1&gt;&gt;</span><em>Autoimmune lymphoproliferative syndrome (FAS)</em>)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 177.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"236\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Splenomegaly, lymphadenopathy, autoimmunity, lymphoproliferation</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.35pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">CHL, nodular lymphocyte-predominant Hodgkin lymphoma, DLBCL, others <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{11418480;21885602;24398331;20216376}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 19; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 27.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"37\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 141.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"188\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>EBV susceptibility, B-cell lymphoproliferation</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 177.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"236\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Impaired elimination of proliferating EBV+ B&nbsp;cells and <em>MYC</em>-rearranged B&nbsp;cells, e.g. <em>SH2D1A</em> (XLP1) <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{9771704}</span>, <em>ITK</em> deficiency <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{19425169}</span>, <em>CD70</em> deficiency, <em>CD27</em> deficiency, <em>MAGT1</em> deficiency (XMEN) <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{32451662}</span>,&nbsp;<em><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-fareast-theme-font: minor-fareast; mso-ansi-language: EN-GB; mso-fareast-language: EN-GB; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA;\">TNFRSF9</span></em><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-fareast-theme-font: minor-fareast; mso-ansi-language: EN-GB; mso-fareast-language: EN-GB; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA;\"> (<em>CD137</em>, <em>4-1BB</em>)</span>&nbsp;deficiency <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{31501153}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 177.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"236\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Severe primary EBV infection (infectious mononucleosis) with HLH; chronic active EBV</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">XLP: BL <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{19874894}</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em>ITK</em> deficiency: EBV+ CHL <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{31057537}</span>, polymorphic or Hodgkin-like lymphoproliferative disorder often involving lung <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{25728094}</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em>CD70</em> and <em>CD27</em> deficiency: EBV+ CHL &gt;&nbsp;EBV+ DLBCL <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{31057537;32603431}</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">XMEN: EBV+ DLBCL, CHL, BL <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{31057537}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 20; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 708.15pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"5\" width=\"944\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Other</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 21; mso-yfti-lastrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 27.9pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"37\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 141.3pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"188\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>SPTCL with germline <em>HAVCR2</em> variants</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 177.3pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"236\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Disinhibited T-cell&ndash;mediated immune response due to loss of function of HAVCR2 (TIM3) <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{30374066}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 177.3pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"236\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Associated with HLH</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.35pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Reported in &gt;&nbsp;50% of patients with SPTCL in predominantly Asian case series <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{34535012;30792187}</span>; can involve mesentery <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{32285995}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">ALPS, autoimmune lymphoproliferative syndrome; AT, ataxia&ndash;telangiectasia; BL, Burkitt lymphoma; CHL, classic Hodgkin lymphoma; DLBCL, diffuse large B-cell lymphoma; EMZL, extranodal marginal zone lymphoma; HLH, haemophagocytic lymphohistiocytosis; LOF, loss of function; NBS, Nijmegen breakage syndrome; SCID, severe combined immunodeficiency; SPTCL, subcutaneous panniculitis-like T-cell lymphoma; T-LBL, T-lymphoblastic lymphoma; XLP, X-linked lymphoproliferative syndrome; XMEN, X-linked immunodeficiency with magnesium defect, EBV infection, and neoplasia.</p>",
